<drawables xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://developer.garmin.com/downloads/connect-iq/resources.xsd">
    <bitmap id="LauncherIcon" filename="launcher_icon.svg" dithering="none" />

    <!-- Media player transport buttons.

         The stock skip art has "30" baked into it, and Garmin's own doc for
         PlaybackProfile.skipBackwardTimeDelta says so: overriding the delta
         "will be necessary to provide a custom icon ... as the default
         indicates 30 seconds". We skip back 10, so the stock button lies.
         SkipButton feeds these to the player through Media.SystemButton.

         ONE ICON PER DISTINCT SCALED DELTA. The app scales the skip by
         playback speed - a 30 s episode-time forward skip is 24 s of a 1.25x
         file, 15 s of a 2x file - and the control dial prints whichever number
         is live. So F<n>/B<n> is the "<n> seconds" glyph, and the iterator's
         forwardArt()/backwardArt() pick the one matching the current track.
         GENERATED by tools/New-SkipIcons.ps1 from the proxy's speed list and
         the base deltas; re-run it and paste its block here if either changes.
         The F30/B10 pair is the speed-100 case and the fallback for any delta
         with no exact art.

         SIZED IN PIXELS, NOT AS A FRACTION OF THE SCREEN. These were 15% and
         22% of screen width, which is what the launcher sizes work out at
         across the 57 products - and it was wrong. Measured on hardware: the
         fenix 7X renders 42/62px correctly, and the fenix 8 CLIPPED the same
         art at 68/100px on the playback screen while drawing it correctly on
         the control dial. If the player's button slot scaled with the screen
         that could not happen, so the slot is near enough a fixed box and the
         art has to be a fixed size too. There is no button size in any
         device's compiler.json - launcherIcon.width is the only icon
         dimension the SDK publishes - so these numbers come from the watch
         and nowhere else.

         Deliberately a little under the fenix 7X's proven 42/62: the cost of
         being small is that it looks small, and the cost of being big is that
         it vanishes.

         DETAIL is the larger image the player draws for a highlighted button,
         so it is bigger than ICON rather than a copy. Both come off the same
         SVG - one art file per glyph. -->
    <bitmap id="SkipF30Icon"   filename="skip_f30.svg" dithering="none" compress="true" scaleX="44" scaleY="44" />
    <bitmap id="SkipF30Detail" filename="skip_f30.svg" dithering="none" compress="true" scaleX="60" scaleY="60" />
